==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|wrh|bilabang}}, likely a compound from {{bor|en|wrh|bila|t=river}} and {{bor|en|wrh|bong}} or {{bor|en|wrh|bung|t=dead}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪləˌbɒŋ/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪləˌbɔŋ/|a=GA}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈbɪləˌbɑŋ/|a=cot-caught}}
* {{audio|en|EN-AU ck1 billabong.ogg|Audio (AU)}}
<!-- no rhymes due to stress -->

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|Australia}} An {{l|en|anabranch}}, {{l|en|backwater}} or {{l|en|oxbow lake}} that is temporarily cut off from the main river, especially one that is only [[filled]] with water during the {{l|en|rainy season}} and can sometimes dry up completely.
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=w:Banjo Paterson|title=w:Waltzing Matilda|year=1895|url=http://www.rogerclarke.com/WM/Manuscript.gif|text=Oh there once was a swagman camped in the '''billabong''',<br> Under the shade of a coolibah tree,<br> And he sang as he looked at the old billy boiling,<br> 'Who'll come a'waltzing Matilda, with me.'}}

